1
00:00:01,700 --> 00:00:06,000
Hi, this is my personal book manager for technology and science fiction.

2
00:00:06,532 --> 00:00:09,892
It runs in the terminal and uses Gum for menus.

3
00:00:09,992 --> 00:00:12,732
And I will demonstrate three operations:

4
00:00:13,032 --> 00:00:16,612
adding a book, searching my library, and getting recommendations.

5
00:00:17,052 --> 00:00:21,412
First, I'll add Dune by Frank Herbert.

6
00:00:21,832 --> 00:00:25,692
The app searches Open Library and shows matching results.

7
00:00:26,512 --> 00:00:30,892
I select the correct book and review the title, author, genre, and link.

8
00:00:31,332 --> 00:00:35,312
I'll mark it as want to read and leave the rating empty.

9
00:00:35,892 --> 00:00:39,132
After I confirm, the app saves the book.

10
00:00:39,172 --> 00:00:43,872
Only the database component reads and writes the CSV file.

11
00:00:44,312 --> 00:00:47,412
Next, I'll search for Frank Herbert.

12
00:00:48,112 --> 00:00:52,472
The book I just added appears with its reading status.

13
00:00:52,812 --> 00:00:55,212
I can also search by title and genre.

14
00:00:55,746 --> 00:01:00,626
The data is saved locally, so my library stays available after I close the app.

15
00:01:01,066 --> 00:01:03,306
Finally, I'll get recommendations.

16
00:01:04,269 --> 00:01:09,689
I'll keep the default interests: programming, AI, and science fiction.

17
00:01:10,209 --> 00:01:14,089
Three recommendation scripts now run in parallel.

18
00:01:14,903 --> 00:01:17,883
History uses my saved books and ratings.

19
00:01:18,509 --> 00:01:20,749
Interests focuses on the topics I entered.

20
00:01:21,289 --> 00:01:24,229
Discovery suggests books outside my usual interests.

21
00:01:25,069 --> 00:01:30,779
The progress messages show when each script is running and when it's finished.

22
00:01:31,219 --> 00:01:36,339
The workflow waits for all scripts, combines their results,

23
00:01:36,639 --> 00:01:41,239
and sends them through a pipe to the refinement script.

24
00:01:41,859 --> 00:01:48,319
The script removes duplicates and books already in my library, then produces a shortlist.

25
00:01:48,759 --> 00:01:52,499
Each recommendation includes a source and a short explanation.

26
00:01:52,939 --> 00:01:59,319
The project is organized into small Bash files, with separate layers for the interface,

27
00:02:00,679 --> 00:02:03,879
workflows, book components, and data storage.

28
00:02:04,590 --> 00:02:06,090
That's my book manager.

29
00:02:06,110 --> 00:02:07,190
Thanks so much for watching.
